  "id": "wernickes-encephalopathy",
  "term": "Wernicke’s encephalopathy",
  "definition": "Wernicke’s encephalopathy is an acute brain disorder marked by eye-movement problems, poor coordination, and changes in thinking or level of consciousness. It is associated with thiamine deficiency and chronic alcoholism, and prolonged thiamine deficiency may progress to Korsakoff syndrome.",
